# STORY-001: The shop-floor interface

machinome-shop is an AI-first CAD software, and the
interface should be unified from the beginning, in the web browser.
That's shop-floor, a software run by codex to provide a web
interface for the user. The user is a maker and is creating a functional
3D printable project.

Codex will be the shop runner, and ideally user only uses codex to open and
close the shop (which means, run the shop floor service and stop it).
For running the shop, codex requires the cheapest/fastest model available.

The shop-floor is a broker between agents and user, and user can see in real
time the whole shop activity, which agents are doing what, inspect designs,
see the functional model live.

The foreman is a subagent running in codex, like all others. User can type instructions
in the floor UI, and user messages are routed to foreman.
User will start codex in a cheap and fast model to run (probably codex-5.3-spark)

The screen is divided in three areas:

- menu: a left column containing online agents and project browsing
- view: an area for visualizing artifacts like machinome widget, design docs etc
- chat: where user types instructions and sees agents activity

## Goals

- Menu show running agents.
  - Orchestrator MUST manifest agent on start and stop
  - Agents appear online waiting as they are launched
  - Agents appear online active when they acquire a task and start work
    - Broker knows when agent acquires a task
    - Agent MUST ack that they got the task (this is start work)
    - Agent MUST report when they finish work, and get back to waiting state
- Viewer shows machinome widget being built by machinist
- Chat allows user interaction
  - User messages are routed to foreman
  - Foreman answers back to user

## Workflow

- User gives instruction to foreman to build
- foreman may interact with user before going if instructions are missing
- foreman sends instructions to designer (renamed from drawing office) and machinist
- designer and machinist work on one instruction cycle each
- foreman keeps user informed and keeps interacting

## Non-goals

- Implementing more project browsing at the menu
- Implement direct interaction between other agents and chat
